==Skills and Abilities==
===First Encounter===
;Azureblight Strafe: During this encounter, Maarselok will fly overhead blasting the ground with his Azure Blight breath attack. If the Azureblight Lurcher is hit by the blast or the lingering Blight damage it will be empowered. 

===Second Encounter===
[[File:ON-creature-Maarselok Unrelenting Force.jpg|thumb|right|Maarselok uses his Unrelenting Force shout]]
;Unrelenting Force: Maarselok with target one player with Unrelenting Force. An alert will pop up on screen and whoever is targeted will see yellow lines coming off of them, similar to the ones seen when an enemy NPC is charging up a heavy attack that must be blocked or dodged. You must either block or dodge Unrelenting Force to prevent being knocked back.
;Summon Stranglers: Maarselok will summon [[Online:Azureblight Strangler|Azureblight Stranglers]] to spit poison at Selene's [[Online:Shagrath's Host|spiders]] as they climb up the blighted vines to reach Maarselok. The stranglers must be killed so the spiders can "convince" Maarselok to come down so the group can damage him. Once he flies down, he will be shrouded in a green aura and stunned for a while. This gives your group the opportunity to damage him, and he will not fight back in his daze. Eventually, he will snap out of it and fly back up to a perch.
;Summon Hoarvors: The Hoarvors that appear during the fight will stun Selene, if she gets hit by their AoE. They need to be killed so Selene can focus on summoning spiders to bring Maarselok down. Optionally, walking into them, will cause them to form an AoE around themselves, and die immediately.
;Summon Lurcher: Every time Maarselok flies up to perch during this encounter, he will summon an [[Online:Azureblight Lurcher]] at his position.

===Third Encounter===
;Summon Wyrm: Summons an [[Online:Azureblight Wyrm|Azureblight Wyrm]]
;Charge: Maarselok rushes forward.
;{{huh}}: Maarselok breathes fire in form of a conical AoE. This can be blocked or dodged.
;Scourge Seed: Maarselok infects one player with the Azureblight. This is indicated by an audio cue. Selene will set down a green rune on one of the stone circles on the ground. When she reveals the infected party member, they will glow blue. That person needs to run over to her ward and cleanse the blight with the synergy.

